Decoder settings for the TrimUI devices (A133, 4x A53):
- avdec_h264_cedar (the Allwinner Cedar hardware H.264 decoder in FFmpeg): no QoS. It only just
  keeps up with 1080p60; QoS made it drop frames after a late one to catch up, which saves nothing
  for a hardware decoder, so it never caught up (two thirds of the frames dropped, mpv: one tenth).
- other avdec_* decoders: max-threads 0 (one per core) instead of 2, which left too little decoding
  power for 720p VP9.

--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/gstreamer/MediaPlayerPrivateGStreamer.cpp
@@ -3748,11 +3748,16 @@
         m_videoDecoderPlatform = GstVideoDecoderPlatform::OpenMAX;
     else if (gstElementFactoryEquals(decoder, "qtic2vdec"_s) || startsWith(name.span(), "c2vdec"_s))
         m_videoDecoderPlatform = GstVideoDecoderPlatform::Qualcomm;
-    else if (gstElementMatchesFactoryAndHasProperty(decoder, "avdec*"_s, "max-threads"_s)) {
-        // Set the decoder maximum number of threads to a low, fixed value, not depending on the
-        // platform. This also helps with processing metrics gathering. When using the default value
-        // the decoder introduces artificial processing latency reflecting the maximum number of threads.
-        g_object_set(decoder, "max-threads", 2, nullptr);
+    else if (gstElementFactoryEquals(decoder, "avdec_h264_cedar"_s)) {
+        // The Allwinner Cedar hardware decoder (FFmpeg h264_cedar) only just keeps up with 1080p60: a
+        // frame that took longer reaches the sink a little late, and QoS then has the decoder drop the
+        // following frames to catch up. That saves no work (the hardware already decoded them), so it
+        // never caught up: two thirds of the frames were dropped where mpv shows 90%. Show late frames.
+        g_object_set(decoder, "qos", FALSE, nullptr);
+    } else if (gstElementMatchesFactoryAndHasProperty(decoder, "avdec*"_s, "max-threads"_s)) {
+        // Software decoders: one thread per core. Two (WebKit's default, for low latency) leave a
+        // 4-core A53 short for 720p VP9; the frame-threading latency is reported to the pipeline.
+        g_object_set(decoder, "max-threads", 0, nullptr);
     }
 
     if (gstObjectHasProperty(decoder, "max-errors"_s))
